**Effect:** The `meta.availableLocales` field returned by these endpoints will now include non-localized media fields (and their folders) via the underlying query. This affects how the admin UI can prefill those media fields when switching/creating locales.

#### 2.2.3 Single-types controller

```ts
// content-manager/server/src/controllers/single-types.ts
import { formatDocumentWithMetadata } from './utils/metadata';

export default {
  async find(ctx: any) {
    // ...
    const version = await findDocument(permissionQuery, model, { locale, status });

    if (!version) {
      if (permissionChecker.cannot.create()) {
        return ctx.forbidden();
      }
      const document = await strapi.db.query(model).findOne({});

      if (!document) {
        return ctx.notFound();
      }

      const { meta } = await formatDocumentWithMetadata(
        permissionChecker,
        model,
        // @ts-expect-error - fix types
        { documentId: document.documentId, locale, publishedAt: null },
        { availableLocales: true, availableStatus: false }
      );
      ctx.body = { data: {}, meta };
      return;
    }

    // ...
    const sanitizedDocument = await permissionChecker.sanitizeOutput(version);
    ctx.body = await formatDocumentWithMetadata(permissionChecker, model, sanitizedDocument);
  },

  async createOrUpdate(ctx: any) {
    // ...
    const document = await createOrUpdateDocument(ctx);
    const sanitizedDocument = await permissionChecker.sanitizeOutput(document);
    ctx.body = await formatDocumentWithMetadata(permissionChecker, model, sanitizedDocument);
  },

  async publish(ctx: any) {
    // ...
    const sanitizedDocument = await permissionChecker.sanitizeOutput(publishedDocument);
    ctx.body = await formatDocumentWithMetadata(permissionChecker, model, sanitizedDocument);
  },

  async unpublish(ctx: any) {
    // ...
    await strapi.db.transaction(async () => {
      if (discardDraft) {
        await documentManager.discardDraft(document.documentId, model, { locale });
      }

      ctx.body = await async.pipe(
        (document) => documentManager.unpublish(document.documentId, model, { locale }),
        permissionChecker.sanitizeOutput,
        (document) => formatDocumentWithMetadata(permissionChecker, model, document)
      )(document);
    });
  },

  async discard(ctx: any) {
    ctx.body = await async.pipe(
      (document) => documentManager.discardDraft(document.documentId, model, { locale }),
      permissionChecker.sanitizeOutput,
      (document) => formatDocumentWithMetadata(permissionChecker, model, document)
    )(document);
  },
};
```

Evidence:
- Uses of `formatDocumentWithMetadata` in `content-manager/server/src/controllers/single-types.ts:5, 57, 96, 137, 180`.

**HTTP routes:** These correspond to admin endpoints like:

- `GET /content-manager/single-types/:model`
- `PUT /content-manager/single-types/:model` (createOrUpdate)
- `POST /content-manager/single-types/:model/actions/publish`
- `POST /content-manager/single-types/:model/actions/unpublish`
- `POST /content-manager/single-types/:model/actions/discard`

Again, confirmed by admin client endpoints that use `collectionType` parameter value of `SINGLE_TYPES`.

**Effect:** Same as for collection-types: single-type metadata now has non-localized media fields populated via `getMetadata`.

### 2.3 Other service consumers of `getMetadata` / `getStatus`

#### 2.3.1 Homepage “recent documents” service

```ts
// content-manager/server/src/homepage/services/homepage.ts
const metadataService = strapi.plugin('content-manager').service('document-metadata');

return {
  async addStatusToDocuments(documents: RecentDocument[]): Promise<RecentDocument[]> {
    return Promise.all(
      documents.map(async (recentDocument) => {
        const hasDraftAndPublish = contentTypes.hasDraftAndPublish(
          strapi.contentType(recentDocument.contentTypeUid)
        );
        const { availableStatus } = await metadataService.getMetadata(
          recentDocument.contentTypeUid,
          recentDocument,
          {
            availableStatus: hasDraftAndPublish,
            availableLocales: false,
          }
        );
        const status: RecentDocument['status'] = metadataService.getStatus(
          recentDocument,
          availableStatus
        );

        return {
          ...recentDocument,
          status: hasDraftAndPublish ? status : undefined,
        };
      })
    );
  },
};
```

Evidence: `content-manager/server/src/homepage/services/homepage.ts:14, 92-120`.

Here `availableLocales` is explicitly `false`, so the new media-population logic still runs (because it’s inside `getMetadata` regardless of options), but its effects only show up in the DB query and not the returned `availableLocales` array (which is ignored). However, the populated media is not consumed here; it’s a minor overhead, not a functional change.

#### 2.3.2 Content history service utils

```ts
// content-manager/server/src/history/services/utils.ts
const getVersionStatus = async (
  contentTypeUid: HistoryVersions.CreateHistoryVersion['contentType'],
  document: Modules.Documents.AnyDocument | null
  ) => {
  const documentMetadataService = strapi.plugin('content-manager').service('document-metadata');
  const meta = await documentMetadataService.getMetadata(contentTypeUid, document);

  return documentMetadataService.getStatus(document, meta.availableStatus);
};
```

Evidence: `content-manager/server/src/history/services/utils.ts:144-162`.

Again, `availableLocales` defaults to `true` in `getMetadata` options (`{ availableLocales = true, availableStatus = true }`), but `getVersionStatus` only uses `availableStatus`. The new media populate logic will still execute; the status computation is unaffected.

This utility is used when building relation responses for history:

