Evidence: `content-manager/server/src/history/services/utils.ts:197-244`.

Net effect: history’s use of `getMetadata` sees the extra media-related populate, but does not use `availableLocales`.

### 2.4 Relations controller uses `getStatus` only

```ts
// content-manager/server/src/controllers/relations.ts
const documentMetadata = getService('document-metadata');

const addStatusToRelations = async (targetUid: UID.Schema, relations: RelationEntity[]) => {
  if (!contentTypes.hasDraftAndPublish(strapi.getModel(targetUid))) {
    return relations;
  }

  const documentMetadata = getService('document-metadata');
  // ...
  return relations.map((relation: RelationEntity) => {
    const availableStatuses = availableStatus.filter(
      (availableDocument: RelationEntity) =>
        availableDocument.documentId === relation.documentId &&
        (relation.locale ? availableDocument.locale === relation.locale : true)
    );

    return {
      ...relation,
      status: documentMetadata.getStatus(relation, availableStatuses),
    };
  });
};
```

Evidence: `content-manager/server/src/controllers/relations.ts:61, 75-107`.

This uses only `getStatus`, not `getMetadata`, so it is **not** affected by the new media-population behavior.

